/-!
# Algebraization of a coherent formal module in cohomological dimension one

Fix an algebraization situation: a Noetherian ring `A` with ideals `I ⊆ 𝔞`, the affine scheme
`X = Spec(A)`, its closed subschemes `Y = V(I)` and `Z = V(𝔞)`, and the open complement
`U = X ∖ Z`.  Let `(ℱₙ)` be an object of `Coh(U, I𝒪_U)`.  [Stacks, Tag 0EJJ] asserts that
`(ℱₙ)` extends to `X` — that is, that it is the restriction to `U` of an object of
`Coh(X, I𝒪_X)` — as soon as

1. `A` has a dualizing complex and `cd(A, I) = 1`, and
2. `(ℱₙ)` satisfies the `(2, 3)`-inequalities of [Stacks, Tag 0EJ3];

and that if moreover `A` is `I`-adically complete then `(ℱₙ)` is the restriction to `U` of the
completion of a coherent `𝒪_X`-module.

The source's proof has four steps.  [Stacks, Tag 0EJG] turns hypothesis (2) into an object
`(ℋₙ)` of `Coh(U, I𝒪_U)` together with a map `(ℱₙ) ⟶ (ℋₙ)` whose kernel and cokernel are
annihilated by a power of `I`, and whose terms satisfy `depth(ℋ_{n,y}) + δ^Y_Z(y) ≥ 3`;
[Stacks, Tag 0EJI] shows that `(ℋₙ)` extends *canonically* to `X` in the sense of
[Stacks, Tag 0EIP]; conclusion (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0EIR] upgrades that to extension to `X`;
and part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0EIU] transports the conclusion back from `(ℋₙ)` to `(ℱₙ)` across
the annihilated comparison.  The final clause is [Stacks, Tag 0EIL].

The tag itself is `Stacks.Algebraization.extendsToX_of_cd_one_of_satisfiesDepthInequalities`,
with its final clause
`Stacks.Algebraization.isCompletion_of_cd_one_of_satisfiesDepthInequalities`, in
`AlgebraizationCdOneTheorem.lean`.  The third step is performed here.  The upgrade from
canonical extension to extension is `Stacks.Algebraization.extendsToX_of_canonicallyExtends`:
the restriction functor `QCoh(X) ⥤ QCoh(U)` carries the pro-isomorphism witnessing canonical
extension to a pro-isomorphism on `U`, by `Stacks.Coherent.nonempty_diagramToPro_comp_iso`;
its target is the pro-object of the termwise restriction of the extension, by
`Stacks.Coherent.coherentAdicPullback_quasicoherentDiagram`; and two objects of
`Coh(U, I𝒪_U)` presenting the same pro-object are isomorphic, by the full faithfulness of
[Stacks, Tag 0EIQ].

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Algebraization.castSystem` — transport of a coherent adic system along an equality of
  ideal sheaves.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.toKerSystem` — a coherent adic system along `I 𝒪_U` read along the
  kernel-ideal-sheaf spelling of that ideal that `Stacks.Algebraization.ExtendsToX` uses.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.extendsToX_of_canonicallyExtends` — conclusion (1) of
  [Stacks, Tag 0EIR], from the comparison of a system with the sheaves associated to its
  global sections.

## Implementation notes

`Stacks.Algebraization.ExtendsToX` and `Stacks.Algebraization.IsRestrictionOfCompletion` are
stated for a coherent adic system along `S.Yι.ker.comap S.U.ι`, the pullback to `U` of the
kernel ideal sheaf of `Y ⟶ X`, while `Stacks.Algebraization.CanonicallyExtends` and the
`(a, b)`-inequalities are stated along `Stacks.Algebraization.idealOnOpen`, the pullback of the
top ideal sheaf generated by `I`.  The two ideal sheaves are equal — that is
`Stacks.Algebraization.ker_Yι_eq_ofIdealTop` — but not definitionally, so the systems are
transported across the equality by `Stacks.Algebraization.toKerSystem`, which changes only the
membership proof and leaves the underlying diagram alone.  Since both predicates mention only
that diagram, the transport is invisible in the statements.

The transport is always performed with the two ideal sheaves as *variables*, by eliminating the
equation between them: that is what `Stacks.Algebraization.castSystem` and the lemmas below
it do.  Done directly on the concrete ideal sheaves of a situation, the resulting
`Eq.rec` makes the kernel unfold `Scheme.ΓSpecIso` and the sheaf of ideals built from it, which
does not terminate within the kernel's budget.

Restriction of a module along an open immersion is `Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor`, which is
what `ExtendsToX` uses, while the pullback functor on coherent adic systems of
[Stacks, Tag 0887] is built from `Scheme.Modules.pullback`; the two are identified by
`Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctorIsoPullback`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EJJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EJJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EHC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EHC), the situation.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EIM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EIM), extension to `X`.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EIP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EIP), canonical extension.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EIQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EIQ), full faithfulness.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EIR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EIR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EIU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EIU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EIL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EIL)
